19^1 &\equiv 19 \pmod{25} \\
19^2 &\equiv 19 \times 19 \equiv 361 \equiv 11 \pmod{25} \\
19^3 &\equiv 19 \times 19^2 \equiv 19 \times 11 \equiv 209 \equiv 9 \pmod{25} \\
19^4 &\equiv 19 \times 19^3 \equiv 19 \times 9 \equiv 171 \equiv -1 \pmod{25}
\end{align*}
\]

From this, we see that $19^4 \equiv -1 \pmod{25}$, so $19^8 \equiv 1 \pmod{25}$. Since 1996 is divisible by 8, we can write $1999 = 100 \times 18 + 7$. Thus, \[
19^{1999} \equiv 19^{100 \times 18 + 7} \equiv (19^8)^{18} \times 19^7 \equiv 1^{18} \times 19^7 \equiv 19^7 \pmod{25}
\]Now we need to find $19^7 \pmod{25}$. We can use the fact that $19^4 \equiv -1 \pmod{25}$ to help us: \[
19^7 \equiv 19 \times 19^6 \equiv 19 \times (19^4)^{1.5} \equiv 19 \times (-1)^{1.5} \equiv 19 \times (-1) \equiv -19 \equiv 6 \pmod{25}
\] Therefore, the remainder of $19^{1999}$ divided by 25 is 6.
